  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Umrao vs State Of U.P. on 19 September, 2019 Author: Sudhir Agarwal Bench: Sudhir Agarwal High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad Court No. - 34 Case :- Criminal Revision No. - 1170 of 1994 Revisionist :- Umrao Opposite Party :- State Of U.P. Counsel for Revisionist :- Pt. Mohan Chandra, Babita Upadhyay, Sanjeev Kumar Gaur Counsel for Opposite Party :- Aga Hon'ble Sudhir Agarwal,J. 1.",
    "facts": "2. This criminal revision under Section 397/401 Cr.P.C., has been filed aggrieved by judgment and order dated 29.07.1994. Thereagainst, accused preferred Criminal Appeal No. 15 of 1994 which was dismissed vide impugned judgment dated 29.07.1994 and confirmed the judgement and order dated 07.02.1994 passed by Court below. Being aggrieved, accused-appellant preferred present revision. It is contended that there was no compliance of Section 13(2) of Act, 1954 and only on the basis that a copy of report was sent to accused and adduced by department as evidence without proving that notice was actually sent to revisionist. Court below has treated to be a compliance of Section 13(2) of Act, 1954 which is wholly illegal, inasmuch as, the law is now well settled for compliance of said section.",
    "arguments": "4. On the question of compliance of Section 13(2) of Act, 1954, I find that Lower Appellate Court has discussed this issue in para-14 which reads as under:- \"14. The learned counsel for the appellant argued that in the present case the provisions of Section 13(2) have also not been complied with. I am fortified in taking above view from recent Supreme Court's Judgement in Vijendra Vs. State of U.P. and others (Criminal Appeal No. 1167 of 2019) (Arising out of S.L.P. (Criminal) No. 4314 of 2015) decided on 31.07.2019. In para 15 of judgment , Court has said as under: \"The very purpose of furnishing such report is to enable the Accused to seek for reference to the Central Food Laboratory for analysis if the Accused is dissatisfied with the report.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The learned counsel for the appellant argued that in the present case the provisions of Section 13(2) have also not been complied with.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "4. On the question of compliance of Section 13(2) of Act, 1954, I find that Lower Appellate Court has discussed this issue in para-14 which reads as under:- \"14. I am fortified in taking above view from recent Supreme Court's Judgement in Vijendra Vs. State of U.P. and others (Criminal Appeal No. 1167 of 2019) (Arising out of S.L.P. (Criminal) No. 4314 of 2015) decided on 31.07.2019. In para 15 of judgment , Court has said as under: \"The very purpose of furnishing such report is to enable the Accused to seek for reference to the Central Food Laboratory for analysis if the Accused is dissatisfied with the report."
  },
